@* An answer that is neither the resource nor a problem: something other than
   a Varve server answered, a proxy or a static host. Said, never blank. *@
<section role="alert" aria-labelledby="no-problem-title">
    <h2 id="no-problem-title">The answer was not one Varve gives</h2>
    <p>
        The address answered <span data-status>@((int)Facts.Status)</span> with neither the resource nor a problem.
        Check that <code>Varve:Server</code> in the Web UI's <code>appsettings.json</code> names the server,
        and that nothing between them rewrites its answers.
    </p>
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>The response's facts.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public ResponseFacts Facts { get; set; }
}
